<title>USA: Maine lawmaker seeks tougher workers' comp bill.</title>
<headline>Maine lawmaker seeks tougher workers' comp bill.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Maine Representative Pam Hatch, D-Skowhegan, introduced legislation that would reinstate a provision of the workers compensation laws requiring employers to pay the legal bills of a worker who wins his or her claim.</p>
<p>Hatch, who said she expects the bill to trigger a major battle, said the reform of the law that eliminated the so-called prevail standard left hundreds of injured workers without proper representation.</p>
<p>But supporters of the 1991 reform law said it is working and Hatch's bill could cause some businesses to leave the state.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
